NAME
       mesg - allow or refuse messages on your terminal

SYNOPSIS
       mesg [y|n]

DESCRIPTION
       mesg controls whether other users can write to your terminal with
       write or wall. "mesg n" refuses, "mesg y" allows; without an argument
       mesg says which is set. Messages from root (such as shutdown
       warnings) always get through.

EXAMPLES
           mesg n

SEE ALSO
       wall(1), write(1)
